 75KR2 H CUT=30-Jun-2013$                                                       
 75KR  Q -7105     8  10063  8  6324   10  -3602   9   2012WA38                 
 75KR cQ $S(2n)=23915 {I10}, S(2p)=10674 {I11}, Q(|ep)=601 {I8} (2012Wa38)      
 75KR c  {+75}Kr produced and identified by 1960Bu22 in bombardment of LiBr     
 75KR2c  with 280 MeV protons followed by measurement of half-life. Later       
 75KR3c  studies of {+75}Kr decay: 1974Ro12, 1974Ho35                           
 75KR c  Note that in many |DJ=1, M1+E2 transitions in the 3/2[301]             
 75KR2c  and 5/2[422] bands, where the mixing ratios seem well measured,        
 75KR3c  the deduced B(E2) values are much higher than the currently            
 75KR4c  RUL(E2)=300 W.u. 1990Sk06 and 1998Sk01 were aware of these anomalous   
 75KR5c  B(E2) values and suggested more precise measurements.                  
 75KR c  Mass measurements using {+78}Kr({+3}He,{+6}He) reaction (1987Mo06)     
 75KR c  Nuclear structure calculations: 1992Ta01, 1987Me09, 1985Ah05, 1985Na02,
 75KR2c  2010Ya13.                                                              
 75KR D  REVIEW OF MOMENTS: 1992Ne09, 1996Li25                                  
 75KR D  YIELDS AND CROSS SECTIONS: 1986Ho22, 1985Hu06, 1982Ba33, 1976La11      
 75KR cG E,RI$Weighted average of available values                              
 75KR2cG when populated in different studies. The average includes the values   
 75KR3cG from {+40}Ca({+40}Ca,4pn|g) which is the most complete dataset but     
 75KR4cG seems to have slightly higher E values (by about 0.5 MeV). Above 2628  
 75KR5cG level, the values are generally from ({+24}Mg,2pn|g),                  
 75KR6cG {+58}Ni({+20}Ne,2pn|g) (1998Sk01) and {+40}Ca({+40}Ca,4pn|g)           
 75KRxcG (2012St19).                                                            
 75KR cG M$From |g(|q) in heavy-ion reactions (1987He01,1990Sk06,1998Sk01)      
 75KR cG MR$From 1998Sk01, unless otherwise stated.                             
 75KR cG E(A)$From ({+54}Fe,2pn|g). Value given in ({+24}Mg,2pn|g) is in        
 75KR2cG agreement but less precise                                             
 75KR cG MR(X)$Note that B(E2)(W.u.) value deduced for this mixing ratio        
 75KR2cG exceeds the currently accepted RUL(E2)=300                             
 75KR cL E$The level structure agrees well among datasets, except for the       
 75KR2cL region above 9 MeV where the structure from {+40}Ca({+40}Ca,4pn|g)     
 75KR3cL (2012St19) was adopted as this is the most complete dataset.           
 75KR cL J$From |g(|q) in (HI,xn|g) and probable band assignment                
 75KR2cL (1998Sk01,1989Ch36,1987He01,1984Ga27,2012St19), unless otherwise       
 75KR3cL stated.                                                                
 75KR cL T$From recoil-distance method (1998Sk01,1990Ca27)                      
 75KR2cL or from Doppler shift attenuation method (2009Tr07),                   
 75KR3cL unless stated otherwise.                                               
 75KR DG CC$ FROM BrIcc v2.2b (20-Jan-2009) 2008Ki07, "Frozen Orbitals" appr.   
 75KR CL BAND(A)$ Ground-state band,|a=+1/2.                                    
 75KR2cL While 5/2[422] is the main configuration, admixture of competing 1qp   
 75KR3cL is likely. Higher members of the band are likely to be of 3qp          
 75KR4cL configuration. For details, see 1998Sk01 and 2009Tr07.                 
 75KR5cL From measured lifetimes (2009Tr07), Q(transition) varies from 3.5      
 75KR6cL to 2.6 b as J|p ascends from 15/2+ to 31/2+.                           
 75KR CL BAND(a)$ Ground-state band,|a=-1/2.                                    
 75KR2cL See comment for |a=+1/2 signature partner.                             
 75KR CL BAND(B)$ Band based on 3/2-,|a=+1/2                                    
 75KR CL BAND(b)$ Band based on 3/2-,|a=-1/2.                                   
 75KR2cL While 3/2[301] is the main configuration, admixture of competing 1qp   
 75KR3cL is likely. Higher members of the band are likely to be of 3qp          
 75KR4cL configuration. For details, see 1998Sk01 and 2009Tr07.                 
 75KR5cL From measured lifetimes (2009Tr07), Q(transition) varies from 3.3      
 75KR6cL to 2.6 b as J|p ascends from 13/2- to 25/2-.                           
